@startuml
actor User
participant FE
participant BE
participant DB

User -> FE : Request file download\n(file shared with them)

FE -> BE : POST /files/{id}/download\n{ password }\n[JWT in header]

BE -> BE : Validate JWT

BE -> DB : Check share entry\n(recipient_id == jwt.user_id\nAND not expired)
DB --> BE : share record + wrapped_FEK

alt no share or expired
    BE --> FE : 403 Forbidden
    FE --> User : Error — access denied or link expired
else access granted

    BE -> DB : Fetch file record\n(\n  ciphertext, nonce,\n  stored_hash, enc_algo, hash_algo\n)
    DB --> BE : encrypted file data

    BE -> DB : Fetch recipient encrypted private key\n(private_key_enc, salt, nonce)
    DB --> BE : encrypted private key blob

    BE -> BE : Derive AES key from password\n(PBKDF2 + stored salt)
    BE -> BE : Decrypt private key blob\n→ RSA private key object

    BE -> BE : Unwrap FEK using recipient\nRSA private key (OAEP)\n→ raw 32-byte FEK

    BE -> BE : Decrypt ciphertext using FEK\n(AES-256-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305)
    BE -> BE : Verify auth tag (tamper check on ciphertext)

    BE -> BE : Recompute hash of decrypted plaintext\n(using stored hash_algo)
    BE -> BE : Compare recomputed hash vs stored hash

    alt hashes match
        BE --> FE : 200 OK — plaintext file bytes\n+ headers: X-Integrity-Check: PASS
        FE --> User : Downloaded file + INTEGRITY PASS
    else hashes differ
        BE --> FE : 422 Unprocessable\n{ integrity: false }
        FE --> User : Warning — file integrity FAILED\n(possible tampering detected)
    end

end
@enduml
